abstract: >-
  A guide and a set of templates for academics, managers, and leaders who want
  to use Claude Code as an executive assistant and project manager, working
  inside their own folders under rules they write. It covers the first hour of
  setup, the three layers of configuration (CLAUDE.md files, memory, and skills
  and scheduled tasks), six hard rules that prevent costly mistakes, the habits
  that let the assistant improve over time, and a first-week plan. The templates
  include a global CLAUDE.md, a work-folder CLAUDE.md, a task workbook, a weekly
  review skill, a morning brief prompt, memory file examples, and a voice
  profile outline. The companion web page adds a guided walkthrough and a
  browser-based builder that writes the CLAUDE.md file.
